.TH HERDR 1 "October 2026" "herdr 0.9.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
herdr \- terminal workspace manager for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B herdr
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B herdr
.BI --session " name"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B herdr
.BI --machine " label-or-id command"
.br
.B herdr
.BI --remote " ssh-target"
.RI [ --session " name" ]
.br
.B herdr
.B session attach
.I name
.br
.B herdr
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B herdr
launches or attaches to a persistent terminal workspace. It can manage
sessions, workspaces, tabs, panes, agents, integrations, and saved remote
machines. It can also run as a headless server or attach to a remote server
through SSH.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [server|client]
Show local client and running server status.
.TP
.B server stop
Stop the running server via the API socket.
.TP
.B server reload-config
Reload the running server configuration.
.TP
.B session attach \fIname\fR
Attach to a named persistent session.
.TP
.B update [--handoff]
Update an installer-managed installation, optionally opting into live handoff.
RPM users must update through their package manager instead
(for example, \fBsudo dnf upgrade herdr\fR).
.TP
.B channel set stable|preview
Select the update channel for an installer-managed installation.
This does not select the RPM package update channel.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Print shell completion definitions.
.PP
Other command groups include \fBmachine\fR, \fBapi\fR, \fBconfig\fR,
\fBworkspace\fR, \fBworktree\fR, \fBtab\fR, \fBnotification\fR,
\fBagent\fR, \fBpane\fR, \fBsession\fR, and \fBintegration\fR.
Run \fBherdr --help\fR for the current command summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --session \fIname\fR
Use or create a named persistent session.
.TP
.B --machine \fIlabel-or-id\fR
Run an API command on a saved SSH machine.
.TP
.B --remote \fIssh-target\fR
Attach through SSH to a remote Herdr server.
.TP
.B --remote-keybindings local|server
Select keybindings for remote app attachment. The default is \fBlocal\fR.
.TP
.B --handoff
Opt into live handoff for update or remote attachment.
.TP
.B --default-config
Print the default configuration and exit.
.TP
.B --skill
Print the agent skill file and exit.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/herdr/config.toml
Default configuration file. The \fBHERDR_CONFIG_PATH\fR environment variable
can override its location.
.TP
.I ~/.config/herdr/herdr.log
Default application log; client and server logs are also written alongside it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HERDR_CONFIG_PATH
Override the path to the configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1)
